lines:
Oh, my, my! Are you traveling alone?
But you’re so young! Good for you!{be01}
I’m sure my kids could learn a thing
or two from you!{be01}
Me? I’m a master of Pokéblocks.{be01}
If I get serious just a little, why, I
can concoct great Pokéblocks.{be01}
Would you like to learn from me, a
master of Pokéblocks?

Oh, good! You’re a smart soul!
This is a bit long, so listen up!{be01}
Are you ready?{be01}
If you look at Pokéblocks, you should see
that they are rated on how they feel.{be01}
The lower the feel rating,
the better it is. Don’t forget this!{be01}
A good Pokéblock has a low feel
rating and a high level.{be01}
A Pokémon can eat more good
Pokéblocks than ordinary ones, too.{be01}
And this is important.{be01}
If you want to make smooth Pokéblocks,
use different kinds of Berries.{be01}
Don’t be stingy - the kinds of Berries
affect the smoothness of Pokéblocks.{be01}
And another thing.{be01}
The more people blending Berries, the
smoother the Pokéblocks.{be01}
That’s why you should talk to other
people and make Pokéblocks together.{be01}
That’s about all you need to know to
make good Pokéblocks.{be01}
If everyone had Pokémon they love,
smooth Pokéblocks, and a loving family,{be00}
the world would be a happier place.{be01}
Don’t give up, dear!
